WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.455
Choose a group of three
There are eight people, and we want a committee of three. There is no chair or
secretary, so the members have identical roles.

2
00:00:13.455 --> 00:00:26.455
Without order or repetition
Answer two questions. Order does not matter, and the same person cannot be
chosen twice. This is an unordered selection without repetition.

3
00:00:26.455 --> 00:00:41.727
Temporarily count with order
If we temporarily count ordered choices, there are eight possibilities for the
first person, seven for the second, and six for the third. Their product is
336.

4
00:00:41.727 --> 00:00:53.364
Remove repeated orders
Each committee has been counted six times because three names have six
possible orders. Correct this overcounting by division.

5
00:00:53.364 --> 00:01:03.182
Find the number of committees
Divide 336 by six to obtain 56 different committees. This agrees with the
combination formula.

6
00:01:03.182 --> 00:01:16.636
Interpret the result
To choose a formula, always ask about order and repetition. Here the result
counts committees. It is neither a probability nor a percentage.
